{
  "_help": "[NOT WIRED YET — design §GM] The hub keepers' real work (Mike, 30 Oct: 'anytime they take action it should be to actually do something for the camp or to make something - not just moving thru the motions'). Keepers work only when a stock they own is below target or an order waits for them; otherwise they rest (§GM.1, §GM.7). All numbers are first guesses for Mike to tune by play. Times (*_min) are real minutes of play: the day is 144 minutes (§GE), with 50–75 of them daylight over the year (§GK.1.2), so a keeper's work has to fit there with rest left over.",

